drm: h713: cover the output height in proc line count

The firmware CalcWindow sequence at 0x8b1a5b90 selects max(input height,
output height). Its movz was previously misread as selecting the minimum,
and Linux programmed the source height for vertical upscale.

A 240-line black source showed a streak near output row 250. Changing only
PROC_FRAME_LINES from 240 to 480 moved it down; 720 removed it, and
restoring 240 brought it back. Match the firmware maximum-height rule,
preserving the upstream start field and the source window and ratio.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@
 #define PROC_PHASE_V		0x38	/* [15:0] */
 #define PROC_RATIO_V		0x3c	/* [21:0] */
 #define PROC_OUT_W_DUP		0x40	/* bit 31 enable, [15:0] width */
-#define PROC_FRAME_LINES	0x50	/* [31:16] start, [15:0] input h */
+#define PROC_FRAME_LINES	0x50	/* [31:16] start, [15:0] max(in h, out h) */
 
 /*
  * DRM expresses plane scale as SOURCE over DESTINATION in 16.16, so a
@@ -439,8 +439,10 @@
 	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_OUT_H, PROC_FIELD16_MASK, out_h);
 	/*
 	 * ProcWinNode::WriteReg writes output width twice and arms the second
-	 * copy with bit 31. More subtly, FRAME_LINES names the number of source
-	 * lines the vertical engine may consume in the low half. Preserve the
+	 * copy with bit 31. CalcWindow sets FRAME_LINES to the larger of input
+	 * and output heights, not the source height alone. Truncating this count
+	 * during vertical upscale produces a visible line-boundary artifact.
+	 * Preserve the
 	 * upper start-line field from the firmware-owned upstream pipeline.
 	 * CalcWindow derives it from input VS delay, upstream vertical start,
 	 * and the MB420 format term. The firmware's 39-line interlaced path
@@ -449,7 +451,8 @@
 	 */
 	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_OUT_W_DUP, BIT(31) | PROC_FIELD16_MASK,
 		      BIT(31) | out_w);
-	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_FRAME_LINES, PROC_FIELD16_MASK, in_h);
+	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_FRAME_LINES, PROC_FIELD16_MASK,
+		      max(in_h, out_h));
 	/*
 	 * ProcWinNode::CalcWindow starts the integer phases at H=3/V=2.
 	 * Unity is the exceptional case that advances each to H=4/V=3 while
